// =========================================================================
// Title: Shearing Image  (SHEAR matrix)
//
// "Animated Images" family: the image of the strip this script is applied
// to (or, if the strip has no image of its own, the surface image) is
// sampled through iChannel0 and transformed by a 2x2 matrix that depends on
// time. The matrix acts on the COORDINATES of the texture plane, which is
// why it is 2x2: it maps (x,y) to (x',y').
//
// TWO CONSTRAINTS OF THIS ENGINE'S SHADERTOY BRANCH:
//  1. the A..F sliders and t can NOT be used here: the engine declares them
//     as LOCAL variables of getCustomColor(), while mainImage() is a
//     separate function -> "'A' : undeclared identifier";
//  2. no MODULE-level declarations (const, functions, #define): with two
//     meshes using this script the fragment would contain two copies of
//     them -> "redefinition", and the surface would disappear.
// That is why the parameters live INSIDE mainImage: there the scope is per
// function and each mesh has its own copy.
// =========================================================================
//
// SHEAR MATRIX: slides the horizontal rows over one another, like a deck of
// cards pushed sideways. Rectangles become parallelograms.
// The determinant is 1 -- the area is preserved -- but the ANGLES are not:
// that is the difference from the rotation, which keeps them.

void mainImage(out vec4 Q, vec2 U)
{
    // --- PARAMETERS (edit here) ---
    float speed = 0.3;    // oscillation speed
    float amount = 0.4;   // how much it tilts

    // Centred coordinate: in the Shadertoy branch iResolution is 1024,
    // so V runs roughly over [-0.5, 0.5].
    vec2 V = U / iResolution.xy - 0.5;

    // Horizontal shear oscillating around zero.
    float g = amount * sin(iTime * speed);
    mat2 M = mat2(1.0, 0.0,
                  g,   1.0);
    V = M * V;

    // Direct sampling, no mip bias: the image stays sharp.
    // +0.5 brings the coordinate back to [0,1].
    Q = texture(iChannel0, V + 0.5);
}
